            <h2 class="sec-title">How Do You Hold the Whole System in Your Head?</h2>
            <p class="sec-lead">Angular SSR involves three separate worlds — a Node.js server, a network, and a browser tab. Each has different rules and different APIs. Two analogies lock the whole system in permanently.</p>

            <!-- Three Worlds -->
            <p style="font-size:.72rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.09em;color:var(--red);text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:.9rem;">First: Every SSR Request Travels Through Three Worlds</p>

            <div style="display:flex;gap:.75rem;align-items:stretch;margin-bottom:1.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;">
              <div class="card" style="flex:1;min-width:160px;border-top:3px solid #7c3aed;text-align:center;padding:1.1rem .75rem;">
                <div style="font-size:1.5rem;margin-bottom:.4rem;">🖥️</div>
                <p style="font-size:.75rem;font-weight:800;color:#5b21b6;margin-bottom:.35rem;">Node.js Server</p>
                <p style="font-size:.68rem;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;">Runs your component code. Builds an HTML string. Has no <code>window</code>, no <code>document</code>, no browser APIs.</p>
              </div>
              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--ink-3);padding:0 .1rem;">→</div>
              <div class="card" style="flex:1;min-width:160px;border-top:3px solid #0284c7;text-align:center;padding:1.1rem .75rem;">
                <div style="font-size:1.5rem;margin-bottom:.4rem;">📡</div>
                <p style="font-size:.75rem;font-weight:800;color:#075985;margin-bottom:.35rem;">Network (HTTP)</p>
                <p style="font-size:.68rem;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;">Carries only plain text — the HTML string. No JavaScript objects, no component state, no functions can travel here.</p>
              </div>
              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--ink-3);padding:0 .1rem;">→</div>
              <div class="card" style="flex:1;min-width:160px;border-top:3px solid #059669;text-align:center;padding:1.1rem .75rem;">
                <div style="font-size:1.5rem;margin-bottom:.4rem;">🌐</div>
                <p style="font-size:.75rem;font-weight:800;color:#065f46;margin-bottom:.35rem;">Browser Tab</p>
                <p style="font-size:.68rem;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;">Receives the HTML string, renders it, downloads Angular JS, then wires Angular logic to the existing DOM.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

