                ];<br/>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ── How the Two Files Work Together ── -->
            <div style="margin-bottom:1.75rem;">
              <p style="font-size:.72rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.09em;color:var(--red);text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:.9rem;">
                How <code style="font-size:.7rem;text-transform:none;">app.routes.ts</code> and <code style="font-size:.7rem;text-transform:none;">app.routes.server.ts</code> Work Together
              </p>

              <p style="font-size:.77rem;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1rem;">
                You do not change your existing <code>app.routes.ts</code> at all. These two files answer
                <em>different questions</em> about the same URL.
              </p>

              <!-- Two-file side by side -->
              <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;margin-bottom:1rem;">
                <div>
                  <div class="code-header">
                    <div class="code-dots">
                      <div class="code-dot" style="background:#ff5f57;"></div>
